      "componentName": "SliceFAQ",
      "items": [
        {
          "_type": "item",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_key": "blk0007",
              "_type": "block",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "spn0008",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "marks": [],
                  "text": "Definica is a hybrid Ethereum-native staking, liquidity, and collateralized borrowing protocol designed around StakeWise-compatible ETH staking infrastructure, osETH composability, Aave-compatible osETH flows, and fixed-duration aEthosETH lock-ups. Each module is activated separately, and the deployed onchain configuration is the final source of truth."
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "style": "normal"
            }
          ],
          "question": "What is Definica?"
        },
        {
          "_type": "item",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_key": "blk0009",
              "_type": "block",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "spn000a",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "marks": [],
                  "text": "No. Eligible deposits are combined in a dedicated StakeWise Vault, and the selected operator runs the validators. Definica Core records your proportional position. Vault capacity, fees and participation conditions are shown before you confirm a transaction."
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "style": "normal"
            }
          ],
          "question": "Do I need to run my own validator?"
        },
        {
          "_type": "item",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_key": "blk000b",
              "_type": "block",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "spn000c",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "marks": [],
                  "text": "Definica uses share-based accounting. Definica Core holds the aggregate Vault position and records each user's proportion. Vault shares are accounting units rather than a fixed one-share-to-one-ETH balance, so your position reflects your share of the Vault and its net performance after protocol and operator fees."
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "style": "normal"
            }
          ],
          "question": "How are my position and rewards recorded?"
        },
        {
          "_type": "item",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_key": "blk000d",
              "_type": "block",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "spn000e",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "marks": [],
                  "text": "StakeWise provides the Vault infrastructure for the pooled staking layer. osETH is StakeWise's liquid staking token, whose exchange rate reflects accumulated staking performance. aEthosETH is the Aave V3 Ethereum aToken for the osETH reserve; supplying osETH to that market creates a position represented by aEthosETH."
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "style": "normal"
            }
          ],
          "question": "Why StakeWise, and what are osETH and aEthosETH?"
        },
        {
          "_type": "item",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_key": "blk000f",
              "_type": "block",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "spn000g",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "marks": [],
                  "text": "In Phase 1 you deposit ETH through Definica Core, which routes eligible ETH to the dedicated Vault and records your position. A withdrawal may use available liquidity or require validator exits before ETH becomes claimable. Phase 2 adds a separate path where eligible osETH is supplied to Aave V3 and the aEthosETH position can be locked in the Main Liquidity Module."
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "style": "normal"
            }
          ],
          "question": "How do deposits, locks and withdrawals work?"
        },
        {
          "_type": "item",
          "answer": [
            {
              "_key": "blk0101",
              "_type": "block",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "spn0101",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "marks": [],
                  "text": "Phase 1 supports optional share locks of 7 to 365 days, with up to 10 lock positions at a time. Locked shares stay in reward accounting. These Core locks are separate from the fixed-duration aEthosETH lock-ups of Phase 2."
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "style": "normal"
            }
          ],
          "question": "Can I lock my Vault shares?"
        },
        {
          "_type": "item",
          "answer": [
            {
